ramwisp — licensing overview
Copyright (c) 2026 Spectre Systems

This repository contains two kinds of code under two licenses:

  mcp/        Apache License 2.0           (see mcp/LICENSE)
  enclave/    Apache License 2.0           (see enclave/LICENSE)
  everything  ramwisp Sustainable Use      (see LICENSE-SUL.md)
  else        License 1.0

In short: the MCP client and the enclave image are fully open source, so anyone can audit the code that
verifies the enclave attestation and rebuild the enclave image to check its published PCR0 hash.

The rest (server, dashboard/site, host agent, infrastructure scripts, brand assets) is source-available:
you may use and modify it for personal, non-commercial, or your own organization's internal use, but you
may not sell it or offer it to third parties as a service. Spectre Systems, as the copyright holder,
operates ramwisp commercially at https://ramwisp.com. For a commercial license, contact Spectre Systems.

The name "ramwisp" and its logos are trademarks of Spectre Systems and are not licensed by either license.
